WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.350
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.025
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.325 --> 00:00:15.100
Unit fourteen: The Human Body. In this unit, you will explain what parts of the body do.

4
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:16.897
Heart.

5
00:00:17.597 --> 00:00:20.409
Heart means the organ that pumps blood around the body.

6
00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:24.427
Your heart beats about 100,000 times a day.

7
00:00:25.127 --> 00:00:27.710
Your turn. Say: Heart.

8
00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:31.214
Heart.

9
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:33.148
Lungs.

10
00:00:33.848 --> 00:00:36.126
Lungs means the organs you breathe with.

11
00:00:36.426 --> 00:00:37.985
Your lungs fill with air.

12
00:00:38.685 --> 00:00:41.232
Your turn. Say: Lungs.

13
00:00:43.932 --> 00:00:44.945
Lungs.

14
00:00:45.950 --> 00:00:46.742
Brain.

15
00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:50.707
Brain means the organ in your head that thinks and controls the body.

16
00:00:51.007 --> 00:00:52.914
The brain controls everything.

17
00:00:53.614 --> 00:00:56.092
Your turn. Say: Brain.

18
00:00:58.792 --> 00:00:59.491
Brain.

19
00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:01.484
Bones.

20
00:01:02.184 --> 00:01:04.741
Bones means the hard white parts inside your body.

21
00:01:05.041 --> 00:01:08.550
Adults have 206 bones.

22
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.949
Your turn. Say: Bones.

23
00:01:14.649 --> 00:01:15.522
Bones.

24
00:01:16.517 --> 00:01:17.599
Muscles.

25
00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:21.494
Muscles means the parts of your body that help you move.

26
00:01:21.794 --> 00:01:23.991
Exercise makes your muscles strong.

27
00:01:24.691 --> 00:01:26.972
Your turn. Say: Muscles.

28
00:01:29.672 --> 00:01:30.720
Muscles.

29
00:01:31.717 --> 00:01:32.648
Stomach.

30
00:01:33.348 --> 00:01:36.334
Stomach means the organ where food goes after you eat.

31
00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:37.937
My stomach hurts.

32
00:01:38.637 --> 00:01:40.941
Your turn. Say: Stomach.

33
00:01:43.641 --> 00:01:44.329
Stomach.

34
00:01:45.317 --> 00:01:46.144
Blood.

35
00:01:46.844 --> 00:01:48.971
Blood means the red liquid in your body.

36
00:01:49.271 --> 00:01:50.794
Blood carries oxygen.

37
00:01:51.494 --> 00:01:53.648
Your turn. Say: Blood.

38
00:01:56.348 --> 00:01:57.047
Blood.

39
00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:58.889
Healthy.

40
00:01:59.589 --> 00:02:02.389
Healthy means in good condition, not ill.

41
00:02:02.689 --> 00:02:04.050
Keep your body healthy.

42
00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:08.099
Your turn. Say: Healthy.

43
00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:11.649
Healthy.

44
00:02:12.650 --> 00:02:14.766
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:15.066 --> 00:02:17.088
Sreypich, what does the heart do?

46
00:02:18.383 --> 00:02:21.210
The heart pumps blood. It helps us live.

47
00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:23.622
And the lungs?

48
00:02:24.917 --> 00:02:26.382
The lungs help us breathe.

49
00:02:27.683 --> 00:02:29.753
Which part do you find most amazing?

50
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:33.760
The brain! It helps us think and remember.

51
00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.060
Grammar focus: The  helps us plus verb.

52
00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:41.511
The heart helps us live. The lungs help us breathe.

53
00:02:41.811 --> 00:02:45.575
After 'help us', use the verb without 'to': helps us breathe.

54
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:49.375
Now read and listen. Our Amazing Bodies.

55
00:02:49.675 --> 00:02:51.245
The human body is amazing.

56
00:02:52.550 --> 00:02:55.409
The heart pumps blood, and the lungs help us breathe.

57
00:02:56.717 --> 00:02:59.691
The brain controls everything, from thinking to dreaming.

58
00:03:00.983 --> 00:03:04.585
Bones and muscles help us move, and the stomach digests food.

59
00:03:05.883 --> 00:03:09.590
To stay healthy, we should eat well, exercise and sleep.

60
00:03:10.883 --> 00:03:13.431
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:13.731 --> 00:03:15.243
The lungs help us blank.

62
00:03:15.543 --> 00:03:18.628
A, breathe. B, to breathe. C, breathing.

63
00:03:22.617 --> 00:03:24.314
The answer is A: breathe.

64
00:03:25.817 --> 00:03:28.199
The organ that pumps blood is the blank.

65
00:03:28.499 --> 00:03:31.746
A, heart. B, brain. C, stomach.

66
00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.970
The answer is A: heart.

67
00:03:39.483 --> 00:03:41.309
The parts that help you move are blank.

68
00:03:41.609 --> 00:03:45.018
A, muscles. B, blood. C, lungs.

69
00:03:49.017 --> 00:03:50.656
The answer is A: muscles.

70
00:03:52.150 --> 00:03:56.219
Now it's your turn to speak. Which part of the body do you find most amazing?

71
00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:06.084
I find the brain most amazing because it helps us think, learn and remember everything.

72
00:04:06.384 --> 00:04:08.105
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:09.117 --> 00:04:13.197
Great work today! You learned eight new words and the  helps us plus verb.

74
00:04:13.497 --> 00:04:17.705
Today's value is self-care. Look after yourself and rest when you are sick.

75
00:04:18.005 --> 00:04:20.971
See you in Unit fifteen. Goodbye!

76
00:04:21.271 --> 00:04:23.621
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

